  }
  .header-title {
    font-size: 14pt;
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  .page-number {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 30px;
    right: 60px;
    font-size: 10pt;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
    <div class="header-logo"><span data-field="company_logo">{{ company_logo }}</span></div>
    <div style="clear: both;"></div>
    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <div class="red-line"></div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 14px; margin: 0;">DESCRIPTIVE BULLETIN</h2>
        <h1 style="font-size: 36px; margin: 10px 0;">SafeGear®</h1>
        <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin: 0;">5/15 kV, up to 50 kA arc-resistant switchgear</h2>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="flex-basis: 60%;">
            <div class="red-line" style="margin-bottom: 0;"></div>
            <h1 style="font-size: 32px; margin-bottom: 15px;">SafeGear® meets today's challenge for improved safety and lower maintenance costs</h1>
        </div>
        <div style="flex-basis: 35%; text-align: right;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 20px;">DESCRIPTIVE BULLETIN</h2>
            <h3 style="font-size: 16px;">Table of contents</h3>
            <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="display: inline-block; width: 40px; text-align: right;">004</span> Medium voltage SafeGear® values and benefits</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="display: inline-block; width: 40px; text-align: right;">005–008</span> SafeGear® overview</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="display: inline-block; width: 40px; text-align: right;">009</span> ADVAC® circuit breakers</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="display: inline-block; width: 40px; text-align: right;">010</span> ADVAC® G40 circuit breaker</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="display: inline-block; width: 40px; text-align: right;">011</span> ADVAC® G50 circuit breaker</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="display: inline-block; width: 40px; text-align: right;">012</span> AMVAC™ circuit breaker</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="display: inline-block; width: 40px; text-align: right;">013</span> Distribution protection and control</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="display: inline-block; width: 40px; text-align: right;">014</span> Switchgear monitoring</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="display: inline-block; width: 40px; text-align: right;">015–016</span> SafeGear® Digital</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
        <div style="flex-basis: 30%;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 18px;">SAFEGEAR® 5/15 kV, UP TO 50 kA ARC-RESISTANT SWITCHGEAR</h2>
        </div>
        <div style="flex-basis: 70%; text-align: right;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 18px;">DESCRIPTIVE BULLETIN</h2>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <div class="two-column-layout">
            <div class="column">
                <h2 style="font-size: 24px;">Medium voltage SafeGear® Values and benefits</h2>
                <p>SafeGear arc-resistant switchgear is available in <span data-field="voltage_levels">{{ voltage_levels }}</span>, and in accordance with <span data-field="standard_reference">{{ standard_reference }}</span>. The short circuit current rating is up to <span data-field="kA_rating">{{ kA_rating }}</span>. SafeGear® offers three different accessibility levels, allowing customers to bring a greater level of flexibility in the marketplace. This differentiates SafeGear® from other arc-resistant switchgear.</p>
                <p>ABB provides solutions for both passive and active arc-resistant switchgear, offering a wide range of solutions for different applications. SafeGear® could be used in <span data-field="application_areas">{{ application_areas }}</span>, including:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li><span data-field="application_list_item_1">{{ application_list_item_1 }}</span></li>
                    <li><span data-field="application_list_item_2">{{ application_list_item_2 }}</span></li>
                </ul>
                <p>The <span data-field="kA_rating">{{ kA_rating }}</span> is available for service voltages of <span data-field="voltage_range">{{ voltage_range }}</span> and all continuous current ratings. The switchgear is designed to meet the highest safety standards, ensuring personnel safety during operation.</p>
                <p>SafeGear arc-resistant switchgear is available in <span data-field="enclosure_types">{{ enclosure_types }}</span>, and is designed to provide the smallest footprint in the lowest cost through reduced building and land costs.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="column">
                <h2 style="font-size: 24px;">SafeGear® Overview</h2>
                <p>SafeGear® meets today's challenge for improved safety and lower maintenance costs.</p>
                <p>No electrical system is foolproof. There's always a chance that insulation system deterioration, equipment malfunction or human error will result in an arc fault. Arc faults can cause severe damage to equipment, personnel, and property. SafeGear® is designed to mitigate the risks associated with arc faults.</p>
                <p>When an arc fault occurs in conventional switchgear, the heat of the arc (<span data-field="arc_heat_temp">{{ arc_heat_temp }}</span> °C) can melt insulation, damage equipment, and cause explosions. SafeGear® is designed to contain the arc within the switchgear enclosure, preventing the heat and pressure from affecting personnel and surrounding equipment.</p>
                <p>SafeGear® arc-resistant construction is designed to contain the arc within the switchgear enclosure, preventing the heat and pressure from affecting personnel and surrounding equipment. The switchgear is designed to meet the highest safety standards, ensuring personnel safety during operation.</p>
                <p>Distribution air faults can cause large amounts of energy to be released into the environment, posing a severe risk to personnel and equipment. SafeGear® is designed to contain these faults within the switchgear enclosure, preventing the release of energy into the environment.</p>
                <p>Components and molten materials are not designed to escape from the switchgear enclosure. The arc does not burn through to adjacent compartments (type 2C and type 2BC) and ground connections remain intact.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
        <div style="flex-basis: 30%;">
