                            <td>8.25</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Rated maximum current</td>
                            <td>kA</td>
                            <td>19</td>
                            <td>36</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Rated short circuit current</td>
                            <td>kA</td>
                            <td>19</td>
                            <td>36</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Rated short circuit current (RMS)</td>
                            <td>kA</td>
                            <td>19</td>
                            <td>36</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Rated short circuit current (peak)</td>
                            <td>kA</td>
                            <td>19</td>
                            <td>36</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Impulse level (BIL)</td>
                            <td>kV</td>
                            <td>95</td>
                            <td>137</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Impulse level (BIL) (RMS)</td>
                            <td>kV</td>
                            <td>95</td>
                            <td>137</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </div>
                <p style="margin-top: 20px;">* Plenum interior</p>
                <p>A system of chambers and tunnels inside the switchgear lineup serves as an exhaust system, allowing the heat generated during an arc fault to be safely vented away from personnel and the affected compartment. Vents</p>
                <p>and flaps are located inside the chamber system and on top of the enclosure to release the pressure. The construction details of this truly innovative con-</p>
                <p>struction details of this truly innovative con-</p>
            </div>
            <div class="column">
                <h2 style="font-size: 24px;">ADVAC® breakers</h2>
                <p>General overview</p>
                <p>The ADVAC® breaker is a spring mechanism breaker with modular, easy to maintain design. Fully compliant with IEEE/IEC 62271-37, the ADVAC® breaker is a great fit for many applications.</p>
                <p>Features:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li>Mechanical anti-plung</li>
                    <li>Arc-resistant</li>
                    <li>Back-to-back C2 cap switch ratings</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Available ADVAC breaker ratings</p>
                <div class="table-container">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Voltage class</th>
                            <th>Nominal voltages</th>
                            <th>Continuous current</th>
                            <th>Short circuit current (kA)</th>
                            <th>BIL (kV)</th>
                            <th>Power frequency</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        {% for row in advac_ratings %}
                        <tr>
                            <td>{{ row.voltage_class }}</td>
                            <td>{{ row.nominal_voltages }}</td>
                            <td>{{ row.continuous_current }}</td>
                            <td>{{ row.short_circuit_current }}</td>
                            <td>{{ row.bil }}</td>
                            <td>{{ row.power_frequency }}</td>
                        </tr>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </tbody>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
        <div style="flex-basis: 30%;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 18px;">SAFEGEAR® 5/15 kV, UP TO 50 kA ARC-RESISTANT SWITCHGEAR</h2>
